    <string name="about_title">About BMI</string>
    <string name="about_message">BMI is your weight in kilograms divided by your height in meters squared. The categories follow the WHO classification of adults (Technical Report Series 894, Table 2.1).\n\nBMI is a screening measure, not a diagnosis. It cannot tell muscle from fat.\n\nThis calculator is for adults aged 20 and over. WHO assesses children and teenagers aged 5 to 19 with BMI-for-age charts instead. The NHS advises against using an adult BMI calculator if you are pregnant, have an eating disorder or have a condition that affects your height.\n\nPeople of South Asian, Chinese, other Asian, Middle Eastern, Black African or African-Caribbean background can face health risks at a lower BMI.</string>
